@@ -18,18 +18,26 @@ rentals.book({ itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-0
 // { id: 'booking-1', itemId: 'board-1', start: '2026-07-01T00:00:00Z', end: '2026-07-03T00:00:00Z', total: 5000 }
 ```
 
-- `addEquipment` takes `{ id, kind, dailyPrice }`, where `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'` and `dailyPrice`
-  is a positive integer number of euro cents per day.
+- `addEquipment` takes `{ id, kind, dailyPrice, hourlyPrice? }`, where `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`,
+  `dailyPrice` is a positive integer number of euro cents per day, and `hourlyPrice`, optional, is a positive
+  integer number of euro cents per hour. An item without `hourlyPrice` can only be rented by the day.
 - `quote` prices a rental without reserving the item. `book` reserves it and returns a booking with an `id`.
-- Periods start and end at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day after the last day. A
-  period that ends where another begins does not overlap it. A rental is priced as whole days times the
-  daily price, reduced by 10% (rounded to the nearest cent, halves up) when it lasts 3 days or more, to
-  reward customers who stay longer. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
-- `availability({ start, end, kind })` returns the sorted ids of the items free for the whole period, of
-  `kind` (`'board'` or `'sail'`) when given and of any kind otherwise. It reserves nothing, so the desk can
-  show what can still be rented before quoting. It throws for a period that is not allowed or an unknown kind.
-- `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period that is not allowed. `book` also throws when
-  the item is already booked for any part of the period.
+- A rental is either whole days or a rental by the hour:
+  - Whole days start and end at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day after the last day. A
+    rental is priced as whole days times the daily price, reduced by 10% (rounded to the nearest cent,
+    halves up) when it lasts 3 days or more, to reward customers who stay longer. Quotes and bookings both
+    show the reduced total.
+  - A rental by the hour starts and ends on the hour (`09:00:00Z`, `12:00:00Z`) and lasts less than a day,
+    so it may cross midnight. It is priced at the hourly price for each hour. Hourly rentals never get the
+    long-rental reduction.
+  - A period of a day or more must start and end at midnight UTC.
+- A period that ends where another begins does not overlap it, whether the periods are by the day or by the hour.
+- `availability({ start, end, kind })` returns the sorted ids of the items free for the whole period and
+  rentable for it, of `kind` (`'board'` or `'sail'`) when given and of any kind otherwise. An hourly period
+  leaves out items without an hourly price. It reserves nothing, so the desk can show what can still be rented
+  before quoting. It throws for a period that is not allowed or an unknown kind.
+- `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item, a period that is not allowed, or an hourly rental of an item
+  without an hourly price. `book` also throws when the item is already booked for any part of the period.
 - Booking ids are sequential within a service (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...), so the same calls always
   give the same ids.
 - Cancellation is not implemented yet.
